PRELUDE spec-mount hook for mle-bench agents/run.py (pinned 507f92e).

mle-bench builds a fixed two-entry volumes_config (read-only data mounts) with
no extra-mount seam, and a `volumes` key in --container-config would collide with
the explicit volumes=. This adds one orchestration hook: if PRELUDE_SPEC_PATH is
set, mount that spec.md read-only at /home/spec/spec.md, which aide-prelude's
start.sh appends as ADVISOR CONTEXT (B/C runs). The agent scaffold and grader are
untouched; the hook is identical across A/B/C, so only the spec content (the
treatment) varies. Applied by setup_cloudbox.sh with `patch --forward --fuzz`.

--- a/agents/run.py
+++ b/agents/run.py
@@ -1,7 +1,12 @@
             "mode": "ro",
         },
     }

+    import os as _os
+    from pathlib import Path as _Path
+    _prelude_spec = _os.environ.get("PRELUDE_SPEC_PATH")
+    if _prelude_spec:
+        volumes_config[_Path(_prelude_spec).resolve().as_posix()] = {"bind": "/home/spec/spec.md", "mode": "ro"}
     container = create_competition_container(
         client=client,
         competition=competition,
